<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Corner mask for the details-page backdrop/trailer card.

     The trailer's TextureView does not follow result_top_holder's outline
     clipping on older GPUs (API 27 era), so a playing trailer renders with
     square corners even though the static backdrop (a normal ImageView)
     is clipped correctly. Instead of relying on clipping, this drawable
     PAINTS the page background colour over everything outside the card's
     24dp rounded corner arc.

     Phase 8.5B geometry (changed from the Phase 7.5 FIX-3 version): the
     mask VIEW (result_top_corner_mask) is now larger than the card — it
     sits in result_top_card_wrap with -12dp margins, so the view's bounds
     are the card rect outset by 12dp on every side. Reason: on device,
     backdrop pixels were escaping the holder's outline clip in a ~6dp
     zone just OUTSIDE the card's top corners (small triangular "ears"
     floating above the card, tinted with the backdrop's own corner
     colours). The old frame-bounds mask could never paint there — its
     bounds ended exactly at the frame edge.

     Construction: a single shape fills the (enlarged) view. Its corner
     radius is 36dp = 24 (card arc) + 12 (view outset), so the shape's
     arc centre coincides with the card's arc centre. The only paint is a
     24dp stroke in ?attr/primaryBlackBackground centred on that outline:
       - inner edge radius = 36 - 24/2 = 24dp: lands exactly on the card's
         corner arc, so within the card the paint covers precisely the
         four corner squares outside the arc (unchanged from FIX-3);
       - outer edge radius = 36 + 24/2 = 48dp: along the straight edges
         the band reaches exactly the view's edge, i.e. 12dp outside the
         card, and diagonally it covers the corner zone out to 48dp from
         the arc centre — the measured ear zone (at most ~11dp above the
         card, hugging its sides) is fully inside the band;
       - the stroke colour is the same attr that result_root and the
         scroll content paint behind the card, in every theme variant,
         so the painted zone is indistinguishable from the page.

     Unlike FIX-3 there are no negative layer insets (the outset now
     comes from the view's own margins), so there is no clamping
     degradation mode. If the view margins were ever lost, the shape
     would be drawn for a card-sized view instead: inner radius still
     24dp but centred 12dp inside the card — corners stay covered, with
     some paint spilling inside the card's straight edges. -->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item>
        <shape android:shape="rectangle">
            <corners android:radius="36dp" />
            <solid android:color="@android:color/transparent" />
            <stroke
                android:width="24dp"
                android:color="?attr/primaryBlackBackground" />
        </shape>
    </item>
</layer-list>
